A trap another core marked hands the processor on as a wait does, and settles nothing,
so a thread a call resumed between the stop and the trap is left ready on no queue, its turn being over, and never runs:
a ready thread that may run waits on its queue.

Caught-by: fuzz-smp2
Report: a place of a ready thread that may run waits on no queue
Witness: fuzz-smp2 cores-resume-before-trap

diff --git a/kernel/core.c b/kernel/core.c
--- a/kernel/core.c
+++ b/kernel/core.c
@@ -211,7 +211,7 @@ struct thread *core_trapped(void)
      */
     core->turn_due = false;
     core->recall = false;
-    sched_turn_end();
+    sched_run_next();
     return NULL;
 }
 
